          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Sometimes true. 9 and 11 are not divisible by 6, 20 is also not divisible by 6. 8 and 10 are not divisible by 6 but 18 is divisible by 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.152,
            0.715,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) Always true. Multiple of 6 = 6x Multiple of 9 = 9y Sum = 6x + 9y = 3(2x + 3y). Hence multiple of 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.236,
            0.852,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) Sometimes true. Multiple of 6 is 18 and multiple of 3 is 9 Sum is 18 + 9 = 27 is a multiple of 9. But multiple of 6 is 12 and multiple of 3 is 9 Sum 12 + 9 = 21 is not multiple of 9 the above cases."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.385,
            0.847,
            0.442
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Find a few numbers that leave a remainder of 2 when divided by 3 and a remainder of 2 when divided by 4. Write an algebraic expression to describe all such numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.449,
            0.848,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let 3a + 2 = x and 4b + 2 = x So, 3a = x – 2 and 4b = x – 2 x – 2 is multiple of 3 and 4. Take LCM of 3 and 4, which is 12 The, first number is x – 2 = 12 or x = 14 = 12 × 1 + 2 Other such numbers are 12 × 2 + 2 =26, 12 × 3 + 2 = 38, … or in general 12n + 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.602,
            0.613,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. “I hold some pebbles, not too many, When I group them in 3’s, one stays with me. Try pairing them up — it simply won’t do, A stubborn odd pebble remains in my view. Group them by 5, yet one’s still around, But grouping by seven, perfection is found."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.636,
            0.598,
            0.83,
            0.713
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.636,
                0.598,
                0.83,
                0.713
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_25_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.743,
            0.846,
            0.788
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "More than one hundred would be far too bold, Can you tell me the number of pebbles I hold?”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.793,
            0.621,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " When group pebbles in 3’s, remainder = 1. Group them by 5, again remainder 1 But grouping by 7, remainder '0 Pebbles are less than 100. LCM of 3, 2, 5 = 30"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.921,
            0.132,
            0.939
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
